==Enemy==
Zollow, despite appearing much later than his living counterpart, has less health and damage than him while also being slower and only having one knockback as well. But don't treat this enemy lightly, as he has both the [[Toxic]] ability and a nasty [[Omni Strike]] attack to compensate. Thanks to his combination of abilities, he can break through meatshield lines and damage your attackers easily. Zollow revives once, but, unlike most Zombies, does not burrow past cats.

His Toxic ability takes off 80% of a cat's maximum health on top of the 10,000 base damage from his attack, instantly killing most units that have under 50,000 health. Anything that isn't immune or resistant to Toxic will be taken out by the second hit.

==Strategy==
This undead bird shouldn't be underestimated. Due to his low health, it is advised to attack him with [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Omni Strike Cats|Omni Strike]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] cats, killing him before he can land a hit. Using [[:Category:Cats with Toxic Immunity|Toxic-immune cats]] like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]], [[Gold Brick Cat (Special Cat)|King Nekokhamen]] (which also resists Floating enemies) and [[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Hades the Punisher]] work great against him, as his damage is not that much of a concern then.

His ability to revive once after death can easily mess up your backliners if they advance; therefore, [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] should be brought to deal with him for good. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] is an excellent choice, as she has Long Distance and can kill him in one hit. Again, Wave Attackers work wonders, as a decent stack of them can cause a Wave right when Zollow revives, killing him just before he deals any damage.

