==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Tebamurasaki Hone Tsubame (テバムラサキホネツバメ), is derived from 手羽先 ''[https://foodinjapan.org/chubu/tebasaki/ tebasaki]'' (a chicken wing dish whose name means "wingtips"), 紫 ''murasaki'' (purple), 骨 ''hone'' (bone) and 燕 ''tsubame'' ([[wikipedia:Swallow|swallow]]).
*His head and, to a lesser extent, his overall body shape when standing upright, are reminiscent of the [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Seventh_Angel Seventh Angel] in ''Rebuild of Evangelion'', often called Clockiel by fans.
*His collapsing and reassembling animations are reminiscent of the [[wikia:mario|Dry Bones]] enemies from the ''Mario'' series. Furthermore, the first stage he appears in is called [[Sodden Bones]], and sodden is an antonym of dry.
*In Greek mythology, the [[wikipedia:Styx|River Styx]] is a river of misery which draws the line between the underworld and the rest of the world.
**Instead of the River Styx, Zollow's Japanese description mentions the [[wikipedia:Sanzu River|Sanzu River]]: a river in Japanese Buddhist tradition which the souls of the deceased must cross before they can reach the afterlife.
*His Japanese description mentions the [[wikipedia:Bon (festival)|Obon festival]], a Japanese annual holiday wherein families return to their hometowns to honor their deceased ancestors.
**In the Taiwanese version, it was localized to the [[wikipedia:Qingming Festival|Qingming Festival]], which has a similar purpose of worshiping one's ancestors; in the Korean version, it's [[wikipedia:Chuseok|Chuseok]], an Autumn harvest festival also known as "Korean Thanksgiving"; in the English version, no festival is mentioned at all.
*The acidic tears mentioned in his Japanese description may be the source of his Toxic ability.
*Prior to [[Version 10.7 Update|Version 10.7]], Zollow wasn't a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy.
*Prior to [[Version 14.2 Update|Version 14.2]], Zollow's English description had a typo. It used to say, "Upset that he can't stop the<b> the</b> mass."
*He has the strongest Toxic ability in the game.

